A Class is a blueprint or template used to create objects.

An Object is an instance of a class.
We create an object by calling the class.

example 1:
class computer:

    def config(self):
        print("i7","16GB","1TB")


com1 =  computer()
com2 = computer()

computer.config(com1)
computer.config(com2)
(or)
com1.config()

